cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite Ticha, the source
  of the manuscript images and transcriptions.
type: software
title: "ticha: Colonial Zapotec manuscripts from Ticha, a line-level HTR dataset and TrOCR models"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-10-25
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Maclenn77/ticha"
authors:
  - family-names: Pérez-Tejada
    given-names: Juan Paulo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-9501-9918"
abstract: >-
  Tools for the Colonial Zapotec manuscripts of the Ticha Digital Text Explorer:
  scrapers for the manuscript list, transcriptions and page images; a pipeline
  that segments pages into lines with kraken and pairs them with their
  transcriptions to build a line-level handwritten text recognition (HTR)
  dataset; and code to train TrOCR on it and read new lines with the fine-tuned
  models.
keywords:
  - Zapotec
  - Colonial Zapotec
  - manuscripts
  - digital humanities
  - handwritten text recognition
  - HTR
  - OCR
  - TrOCR
  - kraken
  - low-resource languages
